{ Hello and welcome to the study! Here I aim to go over basically all the variations of the scotch. We will look at some traps, some gambits, and some other opening things as well!
Before we get started I will ask you to please click the heart bellow. Please enjoy the study! :) }
 *

[Event "Scotch: The Scotch Game"]
[Date "2023.01.29"]
[Result "*"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ECO "C44"]
[Opening "Scotch Game"]
[StudyName "Scotch"]
[ChapterName "The Scotch Game"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/Wr4mGemS/JssaPfIo"]
[Annotator "https://lichess.org/@/Yonushke"]
[UTCDate "2023.01.29"]
[UTCTime "14:09:29"]
[Orientation "white"]

1. e4 { The first move of the Scotch opening is 1.e4.
black plays e5.... } 1... e5 { Here white plays Nf3 as if they are going into a four knights game or Italian game. } 2. Nf3 { Black plays the usual Nc6.... } 2... Nc6 3. d4 { And now instead of a move like Nc3 or Bc4 white immediately strikes in the center with D4. This is called the Scotch game. From here white can go into many different variations, depending on whether they are feeling aggressive or calm. Please go to the next chapter to see the next couple of moves. } *

