1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. Nxd4 Bc5 { Here I will show you another fun trap some players will fall into. } 5. Be3 { Here you play be3, and line up the bishops. } { [%cal Re3c5] } 5... Nf6?? 6. Nxc6 { all of a sudden white wins a piece. } { [%csl Rd8,Rc5][%cal Rc6d8,Re3c5] } 6... bxc6 (6... Bxe3 7. Nxd8) 7. Bxc5 { Here white is up a piece and should be able to quickly win this game, but here is a fun checkmate that could happen. } 7... Nxe4 8. Qd4 { [%cal Rd4e4] } 8... Nf6?? 9. Qe3+ { [%cal Re3e8,Rc5f8] } 9... Qe7 (9... Ne4 10. Qxe4+ Qe7 11. Qxe7#) 10. Qxe7# { and white wins. } *

